  "scope_conclusion": "No demonstrated test-label fitting leakage or numerical kernel defect; conditional original-system integration with modest incremental gains, limited Norman inner contrast support, and no independent optimized neural comparison.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "A01",
      "severity": "material_scope",
      "topic": "conditional core",
      "detail": "Original validation outcomes are reused in all core fits under their historical selection role. Pair OOF targets exclude their own labels, but this is a conditional extension of original v14, not a fully nested refit of all original model-development decisions."
    },
    {
      "id": "A02",
      "severity": "material_scope",
      "topic": "sparse inner contrast support",
      "detail": "Norman seed1 inner dimensions are 1,0,0 and seed3 0,2,2; three of eighteen selection kernels are structurally zero. Weak additional gains cannot establish absence of partner signal."
    },
    {
      "id": "A03",
      "severity": "material_scope",
      "topic": "fixed-G control question",
      "detail": "Lambda is selected for the unit correction, then the same selected G is used for all readout controls. This is valid for a fixed-G control comparison; it does not optimize each policy jointly over lambda and cannot establish their best achievable ordering."
    },
    {
      "id": "A04",
      "severity": "descriptive_diagnostic",
      "topic": "boundary regularization",
      "detail": "All six fits select maximum lambda 10 and all amplitude-only fits maximum tau 16. This suggests unresolved shrinkage scale within the allowed development grid, not numerical convergence failure; no post-test change is licensed as frozen confirmation."
    },
    {
      "id": "A05",
      "severity": "wording_correction",
      "topic": "test access vs computation",
      "detail": "The all-condition half-contract arrays are decompressed before training-row selection. Test entries do not enter fitting calculations, but physical inaccessibility or first-ever test-expression access at scoring is not established. State training-row restriction and prediction-before-scoring sequence."
    },
    {
      "id": "A06",
      "severity": "provenance_improvement",
      "topic": "freeze dependency coverage",
      "detail": "The saved spec directly hashes runner/readout code, while imported core/fast-amplitude/projected-kernel dependencies need source-archive or dependency hashes for a complete freeze. The observed historical source files and exact core replay support current reproducibility."
    },
    {
      "id": "A07",
      "severity": "claim_limit",
      "topic": "gain magnitude",
      "detail": "Selected extension gains are small, and one Norman split selects zero. This supports a callable integration preserving the original core and modest observed gains; it does not constitute a large partner breakthrough or unique readout-agreement mechanism."
    },
    {
      "id": "A08",
      "severity": "claim_limit",
      "topic": "OOF residual interpretation",
      "detail": "Residual targets combine predictions from smaller refitted cores. Their endpoint/baseline coefficients vary between OOF folds; the resulting projected residual can include baseline-estimation variability. The final held-out comparison is valid, but the trained target is an empirical predictive residual rather than an identified molecular-interaction tensor."
    },
    {
      "id": "A09",
      "severity": "wording_precision",
      "topic": "amplitude comparator",
      "detail": "The amplitude-only control uses energy of the projected half-mean, ||(Z1+Z2)/2||². It is not the average of the two half energies, not predicted-effect amplitude, and not a noise-free signal estimate. State its exact formula."
    }
  ],
  "dixit_B_necessary_freeze_points": [
    "Hold each of the 45 canonical pairs out with all its guide/capture/cell records; hide its response from every outer fitting and selection stage. All ten singles may remain available if prespecified.",
    "Use per-cell normalization fixed in advance. Gene-axis selection, variance/HVG ranking and data-derived feature or program standardization must be constructed inside each allowed training set; label-only threefold construction may use all pair identities.",
    "Form disjoint halves within capture (and guide/condition strata where feasible) to avoid artificial capture imbalance. Treat half agreement as within-experiment sampling support, not independent biology.",
    "Fix zero/one/two-target and control-guide multiplicity rules before expression outcomes. Explain whether control is one-NT or two-NT and preserve the same reference across competing predictors.",
    "Use a complete training-only baseline at every nesting depth and rebuild OOF residuals within each partner-training subset. No held inner fold may enter baseline tuning, residual targets, features, shrinkage or initialization.",
    "Freeze whether lambda is selected for unit G before control selection (A-style fixed-G comparison) or jointly by each policy. These answer different questions; B cannot be called an unchanged A learning rule after an unrecorded change.",
    "Keep the common non-target axis for projected loss and a separate per-query mask for full-response MSE. With 10 genes and 5 contrast dimensions per outer fold, 15 total dimensions and 9 overlapping rectangles are not independent replicates.",
    "Hash all imported modeling/preprocessing dependencies and freeze program genes/directions/standardization before evaluating outer test predictions.",
    "Only 10 endpoint clusters limits uncertainty calibration. Use the fixed node-deletion/reweighting sensitivity interpretation; do not assert biological significance, 80% power or general noninferiority from a nominal 45-pair count.",
    "The new experimental source can provide an independent-source, frozen-procedure assessment if its responses were not used for design, while all source data remain retrospective public observations. It is not prospective wetlab confirmation or parameter transfer.",
    "For gene deletion or graph-changing resampling of projected loss, recompute the query incidence projector on each retained graph. Deleting rows after applying the full-graph projector can retain information from removed outcomes; it answers a different fixed-transformation sensitivity question."
  ],
